{"name":"Ash White","hex":"#e9e4d4","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ash","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Abishira."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The solid remains of a fire.","The nonaqueous remains of a material subjected to any complete oxidation process."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ash"},{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ash","blocks":[{"text":"Ash is the solid remnants of fires. Specifically, ash refers to all non-aqueous, non-gaseous residues that remain after something burns. In analytical chemistry, to analyse the mineral and metal content of chemical samples, ash is the non-gaseous, non-liquid residue after complete combustion."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Wood_ash.jpg/330px-Wood_ash.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ash","wikidata":"Q152079"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White","wikidata":"Q23444"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Air_pollution3.jpg/500px-Air_pollution3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Air_pollution3.jpg/1280px-Air_pollution3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Air_pollution3.jpg/500px-Air_pollution3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAir_pollution3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/HK_Sheung_Wan_Wing_Lok_Street_fire_burning_offering_papers_Chinese_style_December_2018_IX2_02.jpg/500px-HK_Sheung_Wan_Wing_Lok_Street_fire_burning_offering_papers_Chinese_style_December_2018_IX2_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/HK_Sheung_Wan_Wing_Lok_Street_fire_burning_offering_papers_Chinese_style_December_2018_IX2_02.jpg/1280px-HK_Sheung_Wan_Wing_Lok_Street_fire_burning_offering_papers_Chinese_style_December_2018_IX2_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/HK_Sheung_Wan_Wing_Lok_Street_fire_burning_offering_papers_Chinese_style_December_2018_IX2_02.jpg/500px-HK_Sheung_Wan_Wing_Lok_Street_fire_burning_offering_papers_Chinese_style_December_2018_IX2_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Joss paper ash. With wind and dispersion, the size of particulates decreases, while the number of particles increases.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHK_Sheung_Wan_Wing